    slug: "lotus-emeya-electric-hyper-gt",
    title: "Lotus Emeya Hyper-GT: 905 HP Dual-Motor Luxury Express",
    excerpt: "Lotus transforms from lightweight sports car specialist into high-performance electric luxury brand. We test the Emeya R's active aerodynamic rear spoiler and 350 kW charging.",
    body: "The transformation of Lotus under Geely ownership is one of the most radical pivots in modern automotive history. The Lotus Emeya is the brand's first four-door electric Hyper-GT, designed to challenge the Porsche Taycan and Audi e-tron GT directly.\n\nIn flagship Emeya R configuration, dual motors and a two-speed transmission deliver **905 HP and 985 Nm of torque**, catapulting the sleek sedan from 0 to 100 km/h in just 2.78 seconds.\n\n![Lotus Emeya Electric Hyper-GT in Solar Yellow | Picture courtesy of Lotus Cars Media](https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1542282088-72c9c27ed0cd?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80)\n\n## Active Aerodynamics: 215 kg of Downforce\n\nThe Emeya incorporates active aerodynamic elements throughout:\n\n- **Active Front Grille:** Shuts to reduce drag (0.21 Cd) or opens to cool the batteries and Brembo carbon-ceramic brakes.\n- **Dual-Layer Rear Spoiler:** 296mm wide active wing generates up to 215 kg of net downforce at high speed.\n- **Active Rear Diffuser:** Extends downward at highway speeds to smooth underbody airflow.\n\nWith a 102 kWh battery pack and 350 kW DC charging capability that takes it from 10% to 80% in 18 minutes, the Emeya is a breathtaking grand tourer for the zero-emission age.",
